[size=200][b]Reference — Core, Dashboard & Settings[/b][/size]
[/align]
[hr]
[size=150][b]Core[/b][/size]
Switch Vision Core provides the Home Assistant integration, automatic Native panel, card runtime, dashboard strategy, asset handling, Calibration backend and shared presentation settings.
Current public Core: [b]v2.6.8[/b]
Protected Gold baseline: [b]v2.5.0 Gold[/b]

[size=150][b]Integration options[/b][/size]
Open:
[code]Settings → Devices & services → Switch Vision → Configure[/code]
Current options include Native/Lovelace sidebar visibility, Calibration buttons, dashboard/card headers, Hub/Installer presentation and Activity LED behaviour.

[size=150][b]Native dashboard[/b][/size]
The Native panel is the recommended dashboard. New cards are prepared before replacing the visible set; a failed refresh leaves the existing cards active.

[size=150][b]Activity LEDs[/b][/size]
Activity intensity is based on traffic relative to negotiated link speed. Controls include Low/Normal/High/Custom sensitivity, Medium/Fast thresholds, Slow/Medium/Fast blink periods, hold time and hysteresis.

[size=150][b]Status information[/b][/size]
Depending on the hardware and available telemetry, Switch Vision can display model, vendor, management address, CPU, temperature, PoE, uptime, OS, firmware, serial, stack state, fans and power supplies.
Missing telemetry is shown as unknown rather than invented.

[size=150][b]Port details[/b][/size]
Depending on source and platform, selected-port information can include VLAN, mode, description, link, RX and TX. Only telemetry actually available from the selected data source should be presented.

[size=150][b]Support-status rule[/b][/size]
The software Gold baseline and hardware support level are independent.
